{title: 578 - So Send I You}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #578 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 578}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]So send I you—by grace made [Fdim]strong to [Gm]tri[C]umph
[C7]O’er hosts of [Gm]hell, o’er [C7]darkness, death, and [F]sin,
My name to [F7]bear, and in that name to [Bbmaj7]con [Gm]quer—
So [D]send [G]I[F]you, My victo[C7]ry to [F]win.
[Bb]“As the [Fmaj7]Father hath [C]sent [F]Me, [Gm7]So[C7]send I [F]you”
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]So send [Fdim]I you- to [Gm]take to [C]souls in bondage
[C7]The word [Gm]of truth [C7]that sets [F]the captive fee,
[F7]To break the [Bbmaj7]bonds of sin, [Gm]to loose dearth's fetters-
[D]So send [G]I you, [F]to bring [C7]the lost [F]to Me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]So send [Fdim]I you- My [Gm]strength to [C]know in weakness,
[C7]My joy [Gm]in grief, [C7]my perfect [F]peace in pain,
[F7]To prove My [Bbmaj7]power, My grace, [Gm]My promised presence-
[D]So [G]send I [F]you, [C7]eternal fruit [F]to gain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]So send [Fdim]I you- to [Gm]bear My [C]cross with patience,
[C7]And then [Gm]one day with [C7]joy to [F]lay it down,
[F7]To hear My [Bbmaj7]voice, 'Well done, [Gm]My faithful servant-
[D]Come, [G]share My [F]throne, My [C7]kingdom, and [F]My crown!'
[Bb]'As [Fmaj7]the [C]Father hath [F]sent [Gm7]Me, so [C7]send [F]I you.'
{end_of_verse}
